DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       llddaappppaasssswwdd  is  a tool to set the password of an LDAP user.  llddaappppaasssswwdd
       uses the LDAPv3 Password Modify (RFC 3062) extended operation.

       llddaappppaasssswwdd sets the password of associated with the user [or an option‐
       ally specified _u_s_e_r].  If the new password is not specified on the com‐
       mand line and the user doesn’t enable prompting,  the  server  will  be
       asked to generate a password for the user.

       llddaappppaasssswwdd  is  neither  designed  nor intended to be a replacement for
       ppaasssswwdd(1) and should not be installed as such.

